==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌtæm.bə.ˈɹiːn/}}
* {{audio|en-us-tambourine.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|tam|bour|ine|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|tambourin||little drum|lang=fr}}, from {{term|tambour||drum|lang=fr}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[percussion]] [[musical instrument|instrument]] consisting of a small, usually wooden, hoop closed on one side with a [[drum]] frame and featuring [[jingle|jingling]] metal disks on the tread; it is usually held in the hand and shaken [[rhythmic]]ally.

====Derived terms====
* [[tambourinist]]

